---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="A Hair's Breadth — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 126"
  description="Chullin 126: a dog that ate from a corpse lies dead across the threshold, and four Tannaim rule on whether the house is impure. Slide the dog, widen its neck, flip it around until the judges say what you need. Then fill Rabbi Shimon's two-of-three grid, scratch a thigh bone and a creeping thing's egg until a hair's breadth of opening flips them impure, and go out and see the orifices, sinews, and seams that decide whether a touch can reach the flesh."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,300..700;1,9..144,300..700&family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="hb min-h-screen">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="hero px-4 pt-10 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm">
          <a href="/daf" class="c-lantern hover:underline">Daf Yomi arcade</a>, Chullin 126, 4 September 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="fr mt-3 text-5xl font-semibold leading-none sm:text-6xl">A Hair's Breadth</h1>
        <p class="frank c-bone mt-3 text-3xl font-bold" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְכַמָּה נְקִיבָתָהּ? כְּחוּט הַשַּׂעֲרָה</p>
        <p class="c-muted mt-1 text-sm italic">
          "And how large must its perforation be? A hair's breadth." Chullin 126b
        </p>
        <p class="c-ink mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed">
          This daf is about openings. A dead dog lies across a threshold with corpse-flesh in its belly,
          and whether the house is impure depends on the width of its neck, the way it faces, and which
          side of the doorstop it lies on. Then the question turns inward: a sealed thigh bone, an animal
          still in its hide, a kidney wrapped in fat, an egg with a creature growing inside. You are impure
          only if a touch can reach the flesh, and a hair's breadth of opening is enough.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-6">
      <!-- ============ Score ============ -->
      <div class="score sticky top-2 z-20 mb-10 flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2">
        <span class="c-muted text-sm">first-try rulings</span>
        <span id="score" class="fr c-lantern text-lg font-semibold">0 / 17</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Act I: The dog on the threshold ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act1-h" class="act">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm italic">The first door</p>
        <h2 id="act1-h" class="fr mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold">The dog on the threshold</h2>
        <p class="frank c-bone mt-2 text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">הַכֶּלֶב שֶׁאָכַל בָּשָׂר מֵת, וּמֵת הַכֶּלֶב, וּמוּטָּל עַל הָאִסְקוּפָּה</p>
        <p class="c-ink mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A dog ate flesh of a corpse, died, and lies on the threshold (Oholot 11:7, quoted on 126a). Four
          Tannaim rule, and each watches a different thing. Rabbi Meir measures the neck. Rabbi Yosei, as
          Rava explains him, measures the empty hollow and where the dog lies against the doorstop line.
          Rabbi Elazar watches which way the impurity will leave. Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira says it leaves
          either way. Arrange the dog until the judges say what each challenge asks for. Some challenges
          cannot be satisfied at all; say so.
        </p>

        <div class="panel mt-5 p-3 sm:p-4">
          <svg id="scene" viewBox="0 0 600 300" class="block w-full" role="img" aria-label="A doorway between the inside of a house and the outside, with a dead dog lying across the threshold stone">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="inside" x1="0" x2="1">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#2a2416" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#171a15" />
              </linearGradient>
              <radialGradient id="glow">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#e2a63d" stop-opacity="0.9" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#e2a63d" stop-opacity="0" />
              </radialGradient>
              <radialGradient id="tumah">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ff8a75" />
                <stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#d05a4e" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#d05a4e" stop-opacity="0" />
              </radialGradient>
            </defs>
            <!-- inside of house -->
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="300" height="300" fill="url(#inside)" />
            <circle cx="90" cy="110" r="120" fill="url(#glow)" opacity="0.35" />
            <!-- outside night -->
            <rect x="300" y="0" width="300" height="300" fill="#0b0f0c" />
            <circle cx="520" cy="58" r="16" fill="#d9d6cc" opacity="0.8" />
            <circle cx="512" cy="52" r="15" fill="#0b0f0c" />
            <!-- door frame -->
            <rect x="228" y="0" width="16" height="230" fill="#3b3225" />
            <rect x="356" y="0" width="16" height="230" fill="#3b3225" />
            <rect x="228" y="0" width="144" height="26" fill="#3b3225" />
            <text x="300" y="18" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b9ad93" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">lintel</text>
            <!-- threshold stone -->
            <rect x="228" y="230" width="144" height="26" fill="#b9ad93" />
            <rect x="228" y="256" width="144" height="44" fill="#8f8570" />
            <text x="300" y="286" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e6dcc6" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif" font-style="italic">threshold</text>
            <!-- shakuf: doorstop line -->
            <line x1="300" y1="226" x2="300" y2="256" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
            <text x="300" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e2a63d" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">doorstop</text>
            <text x="115" y="290" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b9ad93" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif" font-style="italic">inside the house</text>
            <text x="486" y="290" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6f776f" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif" font-style="italic">outside</text>
            <!-- dog -->
            <g id="dog" transform="translate(350 205)">
              <g id="dogflip">
                <!-- tail -->
                <path d="M78 -6 q 28 -22 22 -40" fill="none" stroke="#5b4a35" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <!-- body -->
                <ellipse cx="18" cy="0" rx="62" ry="24" fill="#5b4a35" />
                <!-- legs -->
                <rect x="-20" y="14" width="10" height="20" rx="4" fill="#4a3c2b" />
                <rect x="40" y="14" width="10" height="20" rx="4" fill="#4a3c2b" />
                <!-- neck tube -->
                <g id="neck">
                  <rect id="neck-outer" x="-72" y="-12" width="34" height="24" rx="6" fill="#4a3c2b" />
                  <rect id="neck-inner" x="-72" y="-4" width="34" height="8" rx="3" fill="#1b1611" />
                </g>
                <!-- head -->
                <ellipse cx="-88" cy="-6" rx="22" ry="16" fill="#5b4a35" />
                <path d="M-104 -10 l-16 6 l16 6 z" fill="#5b4a35" />
                <circle cx="-94" cy="-11" r="2.4" fill="#0b0f0c" />
                <path d="M-84 -20 l-6 -12 l10 4 z" fill="#4a3c2b" />
                <!-- impurity in the belly -->
                <circle cx="18" cy="2" r="16" fill="url(#tumah)" />
                <circle cx="18" cy="2" r="5" fill="#ff8a75" />
              </g>
            </g>
          </svg>

          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <p class="c-muted text-xs">How it lies</p>
              <div class="mt-1 flex flex-col gap-1" role="group" aria-label="How the dog lies" data-ctl="mouth">
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="in">mouth inside, rear out</button>
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="out">mouth outside, rear in</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="c-muted text-xs">Its neck</p>
              <div class="mt-1 flex flex-col gap-1" role="group" aria-label="The width of the dog's neck" data-ctl="neck">
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="narrow">under a handbreadth</button>
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="walls">a handbreadth, counting the walls</button>
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="hollow">a handbreadth of empty hollow</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="c-muted text-xs">Where on the stone</p>
              <div class="mt-1 flex flex-col gap-1" role="group" aria-label="Where the dog lies on the threshold" data-ctl="pos">
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="in">past the doorstop, inward</button>
                <button type="button" class="opt" data-v="out">on the outer threshold</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="judges" class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2"></div>
        </div>

        <div id="dog-challenge" class="mt-4"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act II: Two of three ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act2-h" class="act mt-14">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm italic">The second door</p>
        <h2 id="act2-h" class="fr mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold">Two of three</h2>
        <p class="frank c-bone mt-2 text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">שָׁלֹשׁ טוּמְאוֹת פּוֹרְשׁוֹת מִן הַמֵּת, שְׁתַּיִם בְּכׇל אַחַת וּשְׁלִישִׁית אֵין בָּהֶן</p>
        <p class="c-ink mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Rabbi Shimon's baraita (126a to 126b) names three things that come from a corpse and each impart
          impurity in two ways but not a third: contact, carrying, and tent. Each of the three ways is
          missing from exactly one of them. Fill the grid so every row and every column holds exactly two.
          There are several such grids; only one is Rabbi Shimon's.
        </p>
        <div class="panel mt-5 p-3 sm:p-4">
          <div id="grid" class="grid gap-1" style="grid-template-columns: 1.4fr repeat(3, 1fr)"></div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <button type="button" id="grid-check" class="btn">Check the grid</button>
            <span id="grid-msg" class="c-muted text-sm"></span>
          </div>
          <div id="grid-reveal" class="mt-3 hidden text-sm leading-relaxed"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act III: A hair's breadth ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act3-h" class="act mt-14">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm italic">The third door</p>
        <h2 id="act3-h" class="fr mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold">Scratch it open</h2>
        <p class="frank c-bone mt-2 text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">נִיקְּבָה כׇּל שֶׁהוּא – טָמֵא</p>
        <p class="c-ink mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A sealed thigh bone of a carcass and the unbroken egg of a creeping thing with an embryo growing
          inside are both pure to the touch, because no touch reaches the flesh (126b). Perforate them by
          any amount and the touch is impure. Drag across the shell with a single hair. Nothing is scored
          here; this is a toy.
        </p>
        <div class="panel mt-5 p-3 sm:p-4">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1" role="tablist" aria-label="What to scratch">
            <button type="button" class="opt" role="tab" data-obj="bone" aria-selected="true">the thigh bone</button>
            <button type="button" class="opt" role="tab" data-obj="egg" aria-selected="false">the creeping thing's egg</button>
          </div>
          <div class="scratch-wrap relative mt-3 select-none" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9">
            <canvas id="under" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full"></canvas>
            <canvas id="shell" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full cursor-crosshair" aria-label="Scratch surface. Drag to perforate." tabindex="0"></canvas>
          </div>
          <p id="scratch-status" class="mt-3 text-base leading-snug"></p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <button type="button" id="reseal" class="btn">Seal it again</button>
            <button type="button" id="intend" class="btn">I intend to perforate it</button>
            <button type="button" id="tissue" class="btn hidden" aria-pressed="true">embryo tissue: developed</button>
          </div>
          <p id="scratch-note" class="c-muted mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed"></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act IV: Go out and see ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act4-h" class="act mt-14">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm italic">The fourth door</p>
        <h2 id="act4-h" class="fr mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold">Go out and see</h2>
        <p class="frank c-bone mt-2 text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">פּוֹק חֲזִי כַּמָּה נְקָבִים יֵשׁ בָּהּ</p>
        <p class="c-ink mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Rabbi Zeira objected to Abaye: if a covering that blocks touch makes the thing pure, an animal in
          its hide should be pure. Abaye told him to go out and see how many orifices it has. Rav Pappa put
          the kidney in its fat to Rava, who told him to come and see the sinews. Move the lens over each
          case to look for a way to the flesh, then rule.
        </p>
        <div id="cases" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Finish ============ -->
      <div id="finish" class="panel mt-14 hidden p-5 text-center"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="learn-h" class="act mt-14">
        <p class="c-muted text-sm italic">After the game</p>
        <h2 id="learn-h" class="fr mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <ul class="c-ink mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            The dog on the threshold, the four Tannaim, and Rava's rereading of Rabbi Yosei
            (<a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.126a.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">126a:4 to 126a:12</a>).
            The Gemara needs it because Rabbi Yosei had just held that hidden impurity does not break through and rise.
          </li>
          <li>
            Rabbi Shimon's three corpse-sources that impart impurity in two ways but not the third, and why
            this shows he does not treat overlying as touching
            (<a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.126a.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">126a:13 to 126b:4</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            The sealed thigh bone, the hide, the kidney in its fat, and Rav Oshaya on intent
            (<a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.126b.5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">126b:5 to 126b:10</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            The new mishna: the egg with an embryo, the mouse that is half earth, and the sea mouse
            (<a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.126b.11" target="_blank" rel="noopener">126b:11 to 126b:20</a>).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="c-ink mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Read <a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.126a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chullin 126 on Sefaria</a>
          with the commentaries linked to it:
          <a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.126a.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rashi</a> (59 notes; his note on Rava explains the two disputes with Rabbi Meir),
          <a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.126a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Steinsaltz</a> (33),
          <a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin.126a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tosafot</a> (9), and
          <a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Oholot.11.7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mishnah Oholot 11:7</a>
          with the Rash MiShantz (7).
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .hb {
      --night: #101410;
      --panel: #171d18;
      --line: #2a332b;
      --bone: #e6dcc6;
      --stone: #b9ad93;
      --ink: #d9d6cc;
      --muted: #929a90;
      --lantern: #e2a63d;
      --impure: #d05a4e;
      --pure: #62b39a;
      background: var(--night);
      color: var(--ink) !important;
      font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
    }
    .hb .fr { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; color: var(--bone) !important; }
    .hb .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .hb .c-ink { color: var(--ink) !important; }
    .hb .c-muted { color: var(--muted) !important; }
    .hb .c-bone { color: var(--bone) !important; }
    .hb .c-lantern { color: var(--lantern) !important; }
    .hb .c-pure { color: var(--pure) !important; }
    .hb .c-impure { color: var(--impure) !important; }
    .hb h1, .hb h2 { color: var(--bone) !important; }
    .hb p, .hb li, .hb span, .hb div { color: inherit; }
    .hero {
      background:
        radial-gradient(60% 50% at 20% 0%, rgba(226, 166, 61, 0.14), transparent 70%),
        linear-gradient(to bottom, #151a15, var(--night));
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .score {
      background: rgba(23, 29, 24, 0.94);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    }
    .act { border-left: 2px solid var(--line); padding-left: 1rem; }
    .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0.75rem; }
    .lnk { color: var(--lantern) !important; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .lnk:hover { color: var(--bone) !important; }
    .hb .opt, .hb .btn {
      font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: #121713;
      color: var(--ink) !important;
      transition: background-color 120ms, border-color 120ms;
    }
    .hb .opt:hover, .hb .btn:hover { border-color: var(--stone); }
    .hb .opt[aria-pressed='true'], .hb .opt[aria-selected='true'] {
      background: #2b2617;
      border-color: var(--lantern);
      color: var(--bone) !important;
    }
    .hb .btn { background: #1d2620; }
    .hb .btn:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; }
    .hb .opt:focus-visible, .hb .btn:focus-visible, .hb canvas:focus-visible, .hb .cell:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--lantern);
      outline-offset: 2px;
    }
    .judge {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 0.6rem;
      padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
      background: #121713;
      transition: border-color 200ms;
    }
    .judge[data-v='impure'] { border-color: rgba(208, 90, 78, 0.6); }
    .judge[data-v='pure'] { border-color: rgba(98, 179, 154, 0.6); }
    .judge .v { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .judge[data-v='impure'] .v { color: var(--impure) !important; }
    .judge[data-v='pure'] .v { color: var(--pure) !important; }
    .judge[data-v='none'] .v { color: var(--muted) !important; font-size: 0.95rem; font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; }
    .cell {
      aspect-ratio: 2.2 / 1;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      background: #121713;
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--muted) !important;
    }
    .cell[aria-pressed='true'] { background: #24201a; border-color: var(--lantern); color: var(--bone) !important; }
    .cell.good { border-color: var(--pure); color: var(--pure) !important; }
    .cell.bad { border-color: var(--impure); color: var(--impure) !important; }
    .scratch-wrap { border-radius: 0.6rem; overflow: hidden; background: #0b0f0c; border: 1px solid var(--line); touch-action: none; }
    .case { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0.75rem; background: var(--panel); }
    .case svg { display: block; width: 100%; touch-action: none; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: #0b0f0c; cursor: none; }
    .case.done svg { cursor: default; }
    .vbtn { flex: 1; font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 0.5rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #121713; color: var(--ink) !important; }
    .vbtn.pure:hover { border-color: var(--pure); }
    .vbtn.impure:hover { border-color: var(--impure); }
    .vbtn[disabled] { opacity: 0.55; }
    .vbtn.hit { border-color: var(--pure); color: var(--pure) !important; }
    .vbtn.miss { border-color: var(--impure); color: var(--impure) !important; }
    .fb { border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.55; }
    .fb.ok { background: rgba(98, 179, 154, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(98, 179, 154, 0.4); }
    .fb.no { background: rgba(208, 90, 78, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(208, 90, 78, 0.4); }
    #dog { transition: transform 450ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); }
    #dogflip { transition: transform 450ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); }
    #neck-outer, #neck-inner { transition: y 300ms, height 300ms; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      #dog, #dogflip, #neck-outer, #neck-inner, .judge, .opt, .btn { transition: none; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    // ---------- shared ----------
    const TOTAL = 17;
    let score = 0;
    const scoreEl = document.getElementById('score')!;
    const bump = () => { score++; scoreEl.textContent = `${score} / ${TOTAL}`; };
    const sef = (ref: string, label: string) =>
      `<a class="lnk" href="https://www.sefaria.org/${ref}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${label}</a>`;
    let dogDone = false, gridDone = false, casesDone = 0;
    const CASE_COUNT = 9;
    const maybeFinish = () => {
      if (!(dogDone && gridDone && casesDone === CASE_COUNT)) return;
      const f = document.getElementById('finish')!;
      f.classList.remove('hidden');
      const grade = score >= 16 ? 'You measured the hollow, not the walls.' : score >= 12 ? 'Most of the openings found. Go out and see the rest.' : 'The bone is still sealed. Read the daf and scratch again.';
      f.innerHTML = `<p class="fr text-2xl font-semibold">${score} of ${TOTAL} on the first try</p><p class="c-ink mt-2 text-sm">${grade}</p>`;
    };

    // ---------- Act I: the dog ----------
    type Cfg = { mouth: 'in' | 'out'; neck: 'narrow' | 'walls' | 'hollow'; pos: 'in' | 'out' };
    const cfg: Cfg = { mouth: 'in', neck: 'narrow', pos: 'out' };
    type V = 'pure' | 'impure' | null;
    const judges: { id: string; name: string; he: string; rule: (c: Cfg) => [V, string] }[] = [
      {
        id: 'meir', name: 'Rabbi Meir', he: 'רַבִּי מֵאִיר',
        rule: (c) => {
          if (c.mouth === 'out') return [null, 'The mishna puts his case with the mouth facing in.'];
          if (c.neck === 'narrow') return ['pure', 'No handbreadth in the neck, so no tent to carry the impurity in.'];
          return ['impure', 'The neck opens a handbreadth, walls and all, and the whole threshold counts as inside. It draws the impurity into the house.'];
        },
      },
      {
        id: 'yosei', name: 'Rabbi Yosei, as Rava reads him', he: 'רַבִּי יוֹסֵי',
        rule: (c) => {
          if (c.mouth === 'out') return [null, 'The mishna puts his case with the mouth facing in.'];
          if (c.neck === 'narrow') return ['pure', 'Hidden impurity does not break through, and there is no hollow of a handbreadth.'];
          if (c.neck === 'walls') return ['pure', 'We follow the hollow. The walls of the neck do not count toward the handbreadth.'];
          if (c.pos === 'out') return ['pure', 'A hollow handbreadth, but it lies outside the doorstop line, and only the doorstop inward is inside.'];
          return ['impure', 'A hollow of a full handbreadth, lying past the doorstop inward. The house is impure.'];
        },
      },
      {
        id: 'elazar', name: 'Rabbi Elazar', he: 'רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר',
        rule: (c) => c.mouth === 'in'
          ? ['pure', 'The impurity leaves by the rear, and the rear is outside. Food does not go out through the mouth.']
          : ['impure', 'The rear is inside the house, and that is the way the impurity is bound to leave.'],
      },
      {
        id: 'ybb', name: 'Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira', he: 'רַבִּי יְהוּדָה בֶּן בְּתִירָא',
        rule: () => ['impure', 'Either way. It can come out through the mouth or through the rear.'],
      },
    ];
    const heV = (v: V) => (v === 'impure' ? 'טָמֵא' : v === 'pure' ? 'טָהוֹר' : 'not his case');
    const enV = (v: V) => (v === 'impure' ? 'the house is impure' : v === 'pure' ? 'the house is pure' : '');
    const judgesEl = document.getElementById('judges')!;
    judgesEl.innerHTML = judges.map((j) => `
      <div class="judge" id="j-${j.id}" data-v="none">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
          <span class="c-bone text-sm">${j.name}</span>
          <span class="v" dir="rtl" lang="he"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="c-muted mt-1 text-xs leading-snug"></p>
      </div>`).join('');

    const dogEl = document.getElementById('dog')!;
    const flipEl = document.getElementById('dogflip')!;
    const neckOuter = document.getElementById('neck-outer')!;
    const neckInner = document.getElementById('neck-inner')!;
    function renderDog() {
      // The dog drawn facing left (mouth toward the house). Mouth tip sits at x=-120 in local coords.
      const mouthIn = cfg.mouth === 'in';
      // Where the opening that matters sits relative to the doorstop (x=300).
      const target = cfg.pos === 'in' ? 268 : 326;
      let tx: number;
      if (mouthIn) tx = target + 120; // mouth tip at target
      else tx = target - 100; // flipped: rear (x=+100 after flip becomes -100) sits at target
      dogEl.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${tx} 205)`);
      flipEl.setAttribute('transform', mouthIn ? 'scale(1 1)' : 'scale(-1 1)');
      const spec = { narrow: [10, 4], walls: [30, 14], hollow: [34, 26] }[cfg.neck];
      const [outer, inner] = spec;
      neckOuter.setAttribute('y', String(-outer / 2)); neckOuter.setAttribute('height', String(outer));
      neckInner.setAttribute('y', String(-inner / 2)); neckInner.setAttribute('height', String(inner));
      for (const j of judges) {
        const [v, why] = j.rule(cfg);
        const el = document.getElementById(`j-${j.id}`)!;
        el.dataset.v = v ?? 'none';
        el.querySelector('.v')!.textContent = heV(v);
        el.querySelector('p')!.textContent = v ? `${enV(v)}. ${why}` : why;
      }
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ctl]').forEach((g) => {
        const key = g.dataset.ctl as keyof Cfg;
        g.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.opt').forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.v === cfg[key])));
      });
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ctl]').forEach((g) => {
      g.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.opt');
        if (!b) return;
        (cfg as any)[g.dataset.ctl!] = b.dataset.v;
        renderDog();
      });
    });
    renderDog();

    type Want = Partial<Record<'meir' | 'yosei' | 'elazar' | 'ybb', 'pure' | 'impure'>>;
    const challenges: { text: string; want: Want; possible: boolean; why: string }[] = [
      { text: 'Rabbi Meir says the house is impure while Rabbi Yosei says it is pure.', want: { meir: 'impure', yosei: 'pure' }, possible: true,
        why: 'Rava: Rabbi Yosei disputes Rabbi Meir on two counts. A neck that reaches a handbreadth only with its walls satisfies Rabbi Meir and not Rabbi Yosei, and so does a true hollow lying outside the doorstop line.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Meir and Rabbi Yosei both say the house is impure.', want: { meir: 'impure', yosei: 'impure' }, possible: true,
        why: 'Only a hollow of a full handbreadth lying past the doorstop inward satisfies Rabbi Yosei, and that satisfies Rabbi Meir too.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Meir and Rabbi Yosei both say the house is pure.', want: { meir: 'pure', yosei: 'pure' }, possible: true,
        why: 'Under a handbreadth there is no tent for anyone, and hidden impurity does not break through.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Yosei says the house is impure while Rabbi Meir says it is pure.', want: { meir: 'pure', yosei: 'impure' }, possible: false,
        why: 'It cannot be done. As Rava explains him, Rabbi Yosei is lenient on both counts: he needs the hollow itself to be a handbreadth, and he needs it past the doorstop. Whatever satisfies him satisfies Rabbi Meir.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Elazar says the house is pure while Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira says it is impure.', want: { elazar: 'pure', ybb: 'impure' }, possible: true,
        why: 'Mouth in, rear out. Rabbi Elazar follows the way the impurity leaves, which is the rear, and the rear is outside. Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira says it can leave by either end.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Elazar says the house is impure.', want: { elazar: 'impure' }, possible: true,
        why: 'Mouth out, rear in. The rear is inside, and that is the way it is bound to leave.' },
      { text: 'Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira says the house is pure.', want: { ybb: 'pure' }, possible: false,
        why: 'It cannot be done. Rashi: he disputes all of them, mouth in or out, doorstop in or out, a handbreadth or not. The impurity can leave by its way in, or the dog may vomit; either way the house is impure.' },
    ];
    let ci = 0, dogTried = false;
    const dc = document.getElementById('dog-challenge')!;
    const satisfied = (w: Want) => judges.every((j) => !(j.id in w) || j.rule(cfg)[0] === (w as any)[j.id]);
    function renderChallenge() {
      if (ci >= challenges.length) {
        dc.innerHTML = `<div class="fb ok"><span class="c-bone">All seven placements ruled.</span> The judges are done with the dog. Next door.</div>`;
        dogDone = true; maybeFinish(); return;
      }
      const c = challenges[ci];
      dogTried = false;
      dc.innerHTML = `
        <div class="panel p-4">
          <p class="c-muted text-xs">Placement ${ci + 1} of ${challenges.length}</p>
          <p class="c-bone mt-1 text-base">Arrange the dog so that ${c.text}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-a="works">This placement does it</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-a="never">It cannot be done</button>
          </div>
          <div id="dog-fb" class="mt-3"></div>
        </div>`;
    }
    dc.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-a]');
      if (!b) return;
      const c = challenges[ci];
      const fb = document.getElementById('dog-fb')!;
      let ok: boolean, msg: string;
      if (b.dataset.a === 'works') {
        ok = c.possible && satisfied(c.want);
        msg = ok ? c.why : c.possible ? 'Not with this placement. Look at the judges again.' : c.why;
      } else {
        ok = !c.possible;
        msg = ok ? c.why : `It can be done. ${c.why}`;
      }
      if (ok) {
        if (!dogTried) bump();
        fb.innerHTML = `<div class="fb ok">${msg}</div><button type="button" class="btn mt-3" data-a="next">Next placement</button>`;
        dc.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-a="works"],button[data-a="never"]').forEach((x) => (x.disabled = true));
      } else {
        dogTried = true;
        if (b.dataset.a === 'never' && c.possible) {
          fb.innerHTML = `<div class="fb no">${msg}</div><button type="button" class="btn mt-3" data-a="next">Next placement</button>`;
          dc.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-a="works"],button[data-a="never"]').forEach((x) => (x.disabled = true));
        } else if (b.dataset.a === 'works' && !c.possible) {
          fb.innerHTML = `<div class="fb no">${msg}</div><button type="button" class="btn mt-3" data-a="next">Next placement</button>`;
          dc.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-a="works"],button[data-a="never"]').forEach((x) => (x.disabled = true));
        } else {
          fb.innerHTML = `<div class="fb no">${msg}</div>`;
        }
      }
      dc.querySelector('button[data-a="next"]')?.addEventListener('click', () => { ci++; renderChallenge(); });
    });
    renderChallenge();

    // ---------- Act II: two of three ----------
    const rows = [
      { he: 'מְלֹא תַרְוָוד רָקָב', en: 'a ladle-full of corpse mould' },
      { he: 'עֶצֶם כִּשְׂעוֹרָה', en: 'a bone the size of a barley grain' },
      { he: 'גּוֹלֵל וְדוֹפֵק', en: 'the grave cover and its side wall' },
    ];
    const cols = [
      { he: 'מַגָּע', en: 'contact' },
      { he: 'מַשָּׂא', en: 'carrying' },
      { he: 'אֹהֶל', en: 'tent' },
    ];
    // answer[row][col]
    const answer = [
      [false, true, true],
      [true, true, false],
      [true, false, true],
    ];
    const reasons = [
      'Mould imparts impurity by carrying and by tent, not by contact: no one can touch every particle of dust at once.',
      'The barley-grain bone imparts impurity by carrying and by contact, not by tent. A law given to Moses at Sinai.',
      'The grave cover and side wall impart impurity by contact and by tent, not by carrying. Also a law from Sinai.',
    ];
    const state = [[false, false, false], [false, false, false], [false, false, false]];
    const gridEl = document.getElementById('grid')!;
    let html = `<div></div>` + cols.map((c) => `<div class="text-center"><span class="frank c-bone text-lg" dir="rtl" lang="he">${c.he}</span><br><span class="c-muted text-xs">${c.en}</span></div>`).join('');
    rows.forEach((r, ri) => {
      html += `<div class="pr-2"><span class="frank c-bone text-base" dir="rtl" lang="he">${r.he}</span><br><span class="c-muted text-xs">${r.en}</span></div>`;
      cols.forEach((c, cj) => {
        html += `<button type="button" class="cell" data-r="${ri}" data-c="${cj}" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="${r.en}, ${c.en}">–</button>`;
      });
    });
    gridEl.innerHTML = html;
    const gridMsg = document.getElementById('grid-msg')!;
    gridEl.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.cell');
      if (!b || gridDone) return;
      const r = +b.dataset.r!, c = +b.dataset.c!;
      state[r][c] = !state[r][c];
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(state[r][c]));
      b.textContent = state[r][c] ? 'מְטַמֵּא' : '–';
      b.classList.remove('good', 'bad');
      gridMsg.textContent = '';
    });
    let gridTried = false;
    document.getElementById('grid-check')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (gridDone) return;
      const rowsOk = state.every((r) => r.filter(Boolean).length === 2);
      const colsOk = [0, 1, 2].every((c) => state.filter((r) => r[c]).length === 2);
      if (!rowsOk || !colsOk) {
        gridTried = true;
        gridMsg.textContent = !rowsOk ? 'Each of the three must impart impurity in exactly two ways.' : 'Each way must be missing from exactly one of them.';
        return;
      }
      const exact = state.every((r, i) => r.every((v, j) => v === answer[i][j]));
      gridEl.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.cell').forEach((b) => {
        const r = +b.dataset.r!, c = +b.dataset.c!;
        b.classList.add(state[r][c] === answer[r][c] ? 'good' : 'bad');
      });
      if (exact) {
        gridDone = true;
        if (!gridTried) bump();
        gridMsg.textContent = 'That is Rabbi Shimon\'s grid.';
        const rv = document.getElementById('grid-reveal')!;
        rv.classList.remove('hidden');
        rv.innerHTML = `<ul class="c-ink space-y-1">${reasons.map((x) => `<li>${x}</li>`).join('')}</ul>
          <p class="c-muted mt-3">The Gemara's point: mould reaches you through a tent but not by touch, so for Rabbi Shimon overlying and touching are not one category. He is the tanna who disagrees with Rabbi Yosei ${sef('Chullin.126b.4', '(126b:4)')}.</p>`;
        maybeFinish();
      } else {
        gridTried = true;
        gridMsg.textContent = 'Two in every row and column, but not Rabbi Shimon\'s two. The marked cells are wrong.';
      }
    });

    // ---------- Act III: scratch ----------
    const under = document.getElementById('under') as HTMLCanvasElement;
    const shell = document.getElementById('shell') as HTMLCanvasElement;
    const uc = under.getContext('2d')!, sc = shell.getContext('2d')!;
    const status = document.getElementById('scratch-status')!;
    const note = document.getElementById('scratch-note')!;
    const intendBtn = document.getElementById('intend') as HTMLButtonElement;
    const tissueBtn = document.getElementById('tissue') as HTMLButtonElement;
    let obj: 'bone' | 'egg' = 'bone';
    let scratched = false, intent = false, tissue = true;
    const W = 640, H = 360;
    function shapePath(ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      if (obj === 'egg') {
        ctx.ellipse(W / 2, H / 2 + 10, 118, 140, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      } else {
        // thigh bone: shaft with two knobbed ends
        ctx.roundRect(150, 150, 340, 60, 30);
        ctx.moveTo(150, 130); ctx.arc(140, 150, 42, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.moveTo(150, 210); ctx.arc(140, 210, 42, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.moveTo(500, 150); ctx.arc(500, 150, 42, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.moveTo(500, 210); ctx.arc(500, 210, 42, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      }
    }
    function drawUnder() {
      uc.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      uc.save(); shapePath(uc); uc.clip();
      if (obj === 'egg') {
        const g = uc.createRadialGradient(W / 2, H / 2, 10, W / 2, H / 2, 160);
        g.addColorStop(0, tissue ? '#f3b3a4' : '#f0c766'); g.addColorStop(1, tissue ? '#8e4a44' : '#a67c2a');
        uc.fillStyle = g; uc.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
        if (tissue) {
          uc.strokeStyle = '#5a2a2a'; uc.lineWidth = 9; uc.lineCap = 'round';
          uc.beginPath(); uc.arc(W / 2, H / 2 + 10, 58, 0.3, 4.6); uc.stroke();
          uc.beginPath(); uc.arc(W / 2 + 22, H / 2 - 28, 22, 0, Math.PI * 2); uc.fillStyle = '#6a3333'; uc.fill();
          uc.fillStyle = '#1b1611'; uc.beginPath(); uc.arc(W / 2 + 30, H / 2 - 32, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2); uc.fill();
        }
      } else {
        const g = uc.createLinearGradient(0, 150, 0, 210);
        g.addColorStop(0, '#b95f5f'); g.addColorStop(0.5, '#e29a8c'); g.addColorStop(1, '#8a3f3f');
        uc.fillStyle = g; uc.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
        uc.fillStyle = '#e6dcc6'; uc.fillRect(0, 0, 130, H); uc.fillRect(510, 0, 130, H);
      }
      uc.restore();
      uc.fillStyle = '#929a90'; uc.font = 'italic 16px Fraunces, serif'; uc.textAlign = 'center';
      uc.fillText(obj === 'egg' ? (tissue ? 'inside: the embryo' : 'inside: yolk, no tissue') : 'inside: the marrow', W / 2, H - 22);
    }
    function drawShell() {
      sc.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
      sc.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      sc.save(); shapePath(sc);
      const g = sc.createLinearGradient(0, 0, W, H);
      g.addColorStop(0, '#f1e9d6'); g.addColorStop(1, '#c9bda3');
      sc.fillStyle = g; sc.fill();
      sc.restore();
      sc.strokeStyle = '#8f8570'; sc.lineWidth = 3; shapePath(sc); sc.stroke();
    }
    function fit() {
      const r = shell.getBoundingClientRect();
      under.width = shell.width = W; under.height = shell.height = H;
      void r;
    }
    function updateStatus() {
      status.className = 'mt-3 text-base leading-snug';
      if (obj === 'egg' && !tissue) {
        status.innerHTML = `<span class="frank c-pure text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָהוֹר</span> <span class="c-ink">No embryo tissue inside, so it is not a creeping thing at all. Scratch as much as you like; a touch stays pure.</span>`;
        note.innerHTML = `"That creep": just as a creeping thing has developed tissue, so only an egg in which tissue has developed imparts impurity ${sef('Chullin.126b.13', '(126b:13)')}.`;
        return;
      }
      if (scratched) {
        status.innerHTML = `<span class="frank c-impure text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָמֵא</span> <span class="c-ink">Perforated. It only needs a hair's breadth, because a hair can reach the ${obj === 'egg' ? 'tissue' : 'marrow'} through it.</span>`;
        note.innerHTML = `${obj === 'egg' ? 'The mishna: perforated by any amount, impure' : '"Its carcass": what can be touched as carcass, not the sealed bone around it'} ${sef(obj === 'egg' ? 'Chullin.126b.11' : 'Chullin.126b.6', obj === 'egg' ? '(126b:11)' : '(126b:6)')}, and the measure is a hair's breadth ${sef('Chullin.126b.15', '(126b:15)')}.`;
      } else if (intent && obj === 'bone') {
        status.innerHTML = `<span class="frank c-impure text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָמֵא</span> <span class="c-ink">Not yet perforated, but you mean to. Rav Oshaya asked whether a bone that lacks its hole is like something that lacks an act. He answered: it is not. It imparts impurity now.</span>`;
        note.innerHTML = `Rav Oshaya's dilemma and its resolution ${sef('Chullin.126b.9', '(126b:9 to 10)')}.`;
      } else {
        status.innerHTML = `<span class="frank c-pure text-xl" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָהוֹר</span> <span class="c-ink">Sealed. A touch on the ${obj === 'egg' ? 'shell' : 'bone'} reaches no flesh, so the one who touches it stays pure.</span>`;
        note.innerHTML = obj === 'egg'
          ? `The mishna: the egg of a creeping thing in which an embryo has formed is pure ${sef('Chullin.126b.11', '(126b:11)')}.`
          : `"One who touches the carcass is impure", not one who touches a sealed thigh bone ${sef('Chullin.126b.5', '(126b:5)')}. Draw with the hair, or declare your intent.`;
      }
    }
    function resetScratch() {
      scratched = false; intent = false;
      fit(); drawUnder(); drawShell(); updateStatus();
      intendBtn.classList.toggle('hidden', obj !== 'bone');
      tissueBtn.classList.toggle('hidden', obj !== 'egg');
    }
    let drawing = false, last: [number, number] | null = null;
    const toCanvas = (e: PointerEvent): [number, number] => {
      const r = shell.getBoundingClientRect();
      return [((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * W, ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * H];
    };
    function inShape(x: number, y: number) { shapePath(sc); return sc.isPointInPath(x, y); }
    function strokeTo(p: [number, number]) {
      if (!last) { last = p; return; }
      sc.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-out';
      sc.lineWidth = 2.5; sc.lineCap = 'round'; sc.strokeStyle = '#000';
      sc.beginPath(); sc.moveTo(last[0], last[1]); sc.lineTo(p[0], p[1]); sc.stroke();
      sc.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
      if (!scratched && (inShape(p[0], p[1]) || inShape(last[0], last[1]))) { scratched = true; updateStatus(); }
      last = p;
    }
    shell.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { drawing = true; last = null; shell.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); strokeTo(toCanvas(e)); });
    shell.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (drawing) strokeTo(toCanvas(e)); });
    const stop = () => { drawing = false; last = null; };
    shell.addEventListener('pointerup', stop); shell.addEventListener('pointercancel', stop);
    shell.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
        e.preventDefault();
        last = [W / 2 - 40, H / 2]; strokeTo([W / 2 + 40, H / 2 + 6]); last = null;
      }
    });
    document.getElementById('reseal')!.addEventListener('click', resetScratch);
    intendBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { intent = true; updateStatus(); });
    tissueBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      tissue = !tissue;
      tissueBtn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(tissue));
      tissueBtn.textContent = tissue ? 'embryo tissue: developed' : 'embryo tissue: none';
      drawUnder(); updateStatus();
    });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role=tab][data-obj]').forEach((t) => {
      t.addEventListener('click', () => {
        obj = t.dataset.obj as 'bone' | 'egg';
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role=tab][data-obj]').forEach((x) => x.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(x === t)));
        resetScratch();
      });
    });
    resetScratch();

    // ---------- Act IV: go out and see ----------
    type Case = { title: string; he: string; ans: 'pure' | 'impure'; base: string; hidden: string; why: string; ref: string; refLabel: string };
    const S = (x: number, y: number, label: string) =>
      `<circle cx="${x}" cy="${y}" r="7" fill="none" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="${x}" cy="${y}" r="2.5" fill="#e2a63d"/><text x="${x + 11}" y="${y + 4}" fill="#e2a63d" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">${label}</text>`;
    const finger = (x: number, y: number) =>
      `<g><path d="M${x} ${y} l-6 -30 q0 -8 8 -8 q8 0 8 8 l0 30 z" fill="#d9c7a8" stroke="#8f8570" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="${x + 14}" y="${y - 22}" fill="#b9ad93" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">the touch</text></g>`;
    const mouseBase = (fingerX: number, fingerY: number) => `
      <rect x="150" y="70" width="110" height="70" rx="22" fill="#6b5a3f"/>
      <path d="M150 70 h110 v70 h-110 z" fill="#4d3a26" opacity="0"/>
      <rect x="150" y="70" width="110" height="70" rx="22" fill="#7a5a34"/>
      <path d="M205 70 h55 a22 22 0 0 1 0 70 h-55 z" fill="#5a4a30"/>
      <ellipse cx="140" cy="105" rx="22" ry="18" fill="#7a5a34"/>
      <circle cx="132" cy="90" r="9" fill="#7a5a34"/><circle cx="127" cy="104" r="2.5" fill="#0b0f0c"/>
      <path d="M260 110 q40 10 40 34" fill="none" stroke="#5a4a30" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      <path d="M210 80 v60" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 3" opacity="0.5"/>
      <text x="175" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b9ad93" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">flesh</text>
      <text x="235" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b9ad93" font-size="11" font-family="Fraunces, serif">earth</text>
      ${finger(fingerX, fingerY)}`;
    const cases: Case[] = [
      {
        title: 'A carcass still in its hide', he: 'בְּהֵמָה בְּעוֹרָהּ', ans: 'impure',
        base: `<ellipse cx="170" cy="100" rx="90" ry="48" fill="#5b4a35"/><ellipse cx="72" cy="88" rx="30" ry="24" fill="#5b4a35"/><rect x="110" y="135" width="12" height="30" rx="4" fill="#4a3c2b"/><rect x="215" y="135" width="12" height="30" rx="4" fill="#4a3c2b"/><path d="M255 90 q30 -20 24 -44" fill="none" stroke="#4a3c2b" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="170" y="105" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8f8570" font-size="12" font-style="italic" font-family="Fraunces, serif">hide all round</text>`,
        hidden: `${S(62, 80, 'eye')}${S(46, 96, 'nostril')}${S(58, 106, 'mouth')}`,
        why: 'Rabbi Zeira pressed exactly this on Abaye, who answered: go out and see how many orifices it has. The eyes, nostrils, and mouth all reach the flesh.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.7', refLabel: '126b:7',
      },
      {
        title: 'The kidney of a carcass, wrapped whole in its fat', he: 'כּוּלְיָא בְּחֶלְבָּהּ', ans: 'impure',
        base: `<ellipse cx="150" cy="95" rx="92" ry="62" fill="#e6dcc6"/><path d="M118 70 q-30 25 0 50 q20 15 44 0 q22 -20 12 -50 q-24 -20 -56 0 z" fill="#8a3f3f" opacity="0.35"/><text x="150" y="170" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8f8570" font-size="12" font-style="italic" font-family="Fraunces, serif">fat, closed all round</text>`,
        hidden: `<path d="M150 70 q40 -10 70 -30" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/><path d="M158 95 q50 5 80 25" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/><path d="M148 118 q30 30 60 42" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>${S(220, 40, 'sinew')}${S(238, 120, 'sinew')}${S(208, 160, 'sinew')}`,
        why: 'Rav Pappa asked Rava this. Rava: come and see how many sinews run out of it. Each is flesh you can touch.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.8', refLabel: '126b:8',
      },
      {
        title: 'A thigh bone of a carcass, sealed', he: 'קוּלִית סְתוּמָה', ans: 'pure',
        base: `<rect x="70" y="80" width="160" height="34" rx="17" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="68" cy="80" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="68" cy="114" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="232" cy="80" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="232" cy="114" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/>`,
        hidden: `<rect x="90" y="90" width="120" height="14" rx="7" fill="#b95f5f" opacity="0.8"/><text x="150" y="150" text-anchor="middle" fill="#62b39a" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif">marrow inside, no way to it</text>`,
        why: 'The verse says one who touches "the carcass" is impure. A sealed bone is not carcass you can touch, and the marrow cannot be reached.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.5', refLabel: '126b:5 to 6',
      },
      {
        title: 'The same thigh bone, with a hole a hair wide', he: 'קוּלִית נְקוּבָה', ans: 'impure',
        base: `<rect x="70" y="80" width="160" height="34" rx="17" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="68" cy="80" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="68" cy="114" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="232" cy="80" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="232" cy="114" r="22" fill="#e6dcc6"/><circle cx="160" cy="97" r="0.8" fill="#8a3f3f"/>`,
        hidden: `<rect x="90" y="90" width="120" height="14" rx="7" fill="#b95f5f" opacity="0.8"/><line x1="160" y1="30" x2="160" y2="97" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="0.8"/>${S(160, 97, 'a hair fits through')}`,
        why: 'Perforated, a touch can reach the marrow, and the measure is the width of a hair, because a hair can pass through.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.15', refLabel: '126b:15',
      },
      {
        title: 'A creeping thing\'s egg with an embryo inside, unbroken', he: 'בֵּיצַת הַשֶּׁרֶץ הַמְרוּקֶּמֶת', ans: 'pure',
        base: `<ellipse cx="150" cy="95" rx="58" ry="72" fill="#efe6d1"/>`,
        hidden: `<path d="M150 95 m-28 0 a28 28 0 1 1 28 28" fill="none" stroke="#8a3f3f" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.8"/><text x="150" y="182" text-anchor="middle" fill="#62b39a" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif">tissue inside, shell whole</text>`,
        why: 'The mishna: the egg of a creeping thing in which tissue has formed is pure, because the creeping thing is sealed away.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.11', refLabel: '126b:11',
      },
      {
        title: 'An egg with no embryo tissue, cracked open', he: 'בֵּיצָה שֶׁאֵינָהּ מְרוּקֶּמֶת', ans: 'pure',
        base: `<ellipse cx="150" cy="95" rx="58" ry="72" fill="#efe6d1"/><path d="M118 60 l14 10 l-8 12 l16 8 l-6 14" fill="none" stroke="#5b4a35" stroke-width="2"/>`,
        hidden: `<circle cx="150" cy="100" r="22" fill="#f0c766" opacity="0.9"/><text x="150" y="182" text-anchor="middle" fill="#62b39a" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif">open, but only yolk inside</text>`,
        why: '"That creep": just as a creeping thing has developed tissue, so only an egg with developed tissue imparts impurity. An opening with no creature behind it is nothing.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.13', refLabel: '126b:13',
      },
      {
        title: 'A mouse that is half flesh and half earth: you touch the earth, away from the flesh', he: 'עַכְבָּר שֶׁחֶצְיוֹ בָּשָׂר וְחֶצְיוֹ אֲדָמָה', ans: 'pure',
        base: mouseBase(248, 118),
        hidden: `<line x1="210" y1="66" x2="210" y2="146" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5"/>${S(210, 60, 'the seam')}`,
        why: 'The mishna: one who touches the flesh is impure, the earth pure. Rabbi Yehuda adds only the earth directly against the flesh; this touch is well away from it.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.11', refLabel: '126b:11',
      },
      {
        title: 'The same half-earth mouse: you touch the flesh half', he: 'הַנּוֹגֵעַ בַּבָּשָׂר', ans: 'impure',
        base: mouseBase(178, 118),
        hidden: `<line x1="210" y1="66" x2="210" y2="146" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5"/>${S(178, 76, 'flesh')}`,
        why: 'The mishna\'s first clause: one who touches the flesh is impure. Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi, in one version, adds that the flesh must have formed from head to foot along its length.', ref: 'Chullin.126b.16', refLabel: '126b:16 to 17',
      },
      {
        title: 'A sea mouse, dead, in your hand', he: 'עַכְבָּר שֶׁבַּיָּם', ans: 'pure',
        base: `<path d="M0 150 q30 -12 60 0 t60 0 t60 0 t60 0 t60 0 v50 h-300 z" fill="#1d3a3a"/><rect x="120" y="80" width="90" height="52" rx="20" fill="#5a6f6f"/><ellipse cx="112" cy="106" rx="18" ry="15" fill="#5a6f6f"/><circle cx="100" cy="103" r="2.5" fill="#0b0f0c"/><path d="M160 80 l14 -18 l8 18 z" fill="#4b5c5c"/><path d="M210 106 l26 -14 v28 z" fill="#4b5c5c"/>`,
        hidden: `<text x="150" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#62b39a" font-size="12" font-family="Fraunces, serif">"upon the earth", not in the sea</text>${S(174, 66, 'fin')}`,
        why: 'The baraita: "mouse" might have meant anything called a mouse, even the sea mouse, or only a land-grower like the weasel. The verse settles it with "upon the earth".', ref: 'Chullin.126b.18', refLabel: '126b:18 to 19',
      },
    ];
    const casesEl = document.getElementById('cases')!;
    casesEl.innerHTML = cases.map((c, i) => `
      <div class="case p-3 sm:p-4" data-i="${i}">
        <p class="c-bone text-base">${c.title}</p>
        <p class="frank c-muted text-lg" dir="rtl" lang="he">${c.he}</p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 200" class="mt-2" role="img" aria-label="${c.title}">
          <defs><clipPath id="lens-${i}"><circle class="lens-clip" cx="-100" cy="-100" r="42"/></clipPath></defs>
          ${c.base}
          <g clip-path="url(#lens-${i})" class="hidden-layer">${c.hidden}</g>
          <circle class="lens-ring" cx="-100" cy="-100" r="42" fill="none" stroke="#e2a63d" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.9"/>
        </svg>
        <div class="mt-2 flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="c-muted text-xs">Move the lens to look for an opening.</span>
          <button type="button" class="btn text-xs" data-reveal>Show everything</button>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3 flex gap-2">
          <button type="button" class="vbtn pure" data-v="pure" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָהוֹר</button>
          <button type="button" class="vbtn impure" data-v="impure" dir="rtl" lang="he">טָמֵא</button>
        </div>
        <div class="fbwrap mt-3"></div>
      </div>`).join('');
    casesEl.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.case').forEach((card) => {
      const svg = card.querySelector('svg')!;
      const clip = svg.querySelector<SVGCircleElement>('.lens-clip')!;
      const ring = svg.querySelector<SVGCircleElement>('.lens-ring')!;
      const move = (e: PointerEvent) => {
        const r = svg.getBoundingClientRect();
        const x = ((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * 300, y = ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * 200;
        clip.setAttribute('cx', String(x)); clip.setAttribute('cy', String(y));
        ring.setAttribute('cx', String(x)); ring.setAttribute('cy', String(y));
      };
      svg.addEventListener('pointermove', move);
      svg.addEventListener('pointerdown', move);
      const revealAll = () => {
        svg.querySelector('.hidden-layer')!.removeAttribute('clip-path');
        ring.setAttribute('opacity', '0');
        svg.removeEventListener('pointermove', move);
        card.classList.add('done');
      };
      card.querySelector('[data-reveal]')!.addEventListener('click', revealAll);
      const i = +card.dataset.i!;
      const c = cases[i];
      card.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.vbtn').forEach((b) => {
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const ok = b.dataset.v === c.ans;
          card.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.vbtn').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (x.dataset.v === c.ans) x.classList.add('hit'); });
          if (!ok) b.classList.add('miss'); else bump();
          revealAll();
          card.querySelector('.fbwrap')!.innerHTML = `<div class="fb ${ok ? 'ok' : 'no'}"><span class="frank ${c.ans === 'pure' ? 'c-pure' : 'c-impure'}" dir="rtl" lang="he">${c.ans === 'pure' ? 'טָהוֹר' : 'טָמֵא'}</span> ${c.why} ${sef(c.ref, `(${c.refLabel})`)}</div>`;
          casesDone++; maybeFinish();
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
